\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Takeaway: one explanation; three predictions and a mechanism probe confirmed; and one falsified scope prediction whose revised boundary hypothesis was then tested held-out, with a split verdict.} The explanation is that a reference on a multi-valid task is one sample from the valid set and the judge anchors on it. Anchoring is in points of the judge's 0--10 scale; inflation and the training wedge are in baseline standard deviations of the judge's own score distribution. Intervals, caveats, and the predictions that failed are in the sections named.}}{2}{table.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
